  "auth-oauth-server": [
    {
      id: "US-AUTH-OAUTH-SERVER",
      title: "Sovrium acts as an OAuth 2.1 / OIDC 1.0 authorization server",
      criteria: [
        "When `app.auth` is configured, `GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server` returns a valid RFC 8414 metadata document with `S256` advertised",
        "The metadata document advertises `authorization_endpoint`, `token_endpoint`, `registration_endpoint` URIs on the same host as `issuer`",
        "A signed-in user may register a client dynamically (RFC 7591) and receives a `client_id` (and a `client_secret` only for confidential clients)",
        "`GET /api/auth/oauth2/authorize` without a `code_challenge` returns `error=invalid_request` (PKCE required by OAuth 2.1)",
        "`GET /api/auth/oauth2/authorize` with `code_challenge_method=plain` returns `error=invalid_request` (S256 only)",
        "The full PKCE-S256 authorization-code flow exchanges a code for an access token at `/api/auth/oauth2/token` (with `id_token` if `openid` scope)",
        "Introspecting an issued access token (RFC 7662) returns `active=true` with `sub` matching `auth.user.id` and `client_id` echoed",
        "`POST /api/auth/oauth2/revoke` (RFC 7009) revokes an access token; subsequent introspection returns `active=false`",
        "When `app.auth` is NOT configured, OAuth-server endpoints return 404 (plugin not mounted)",
        "`GET /.well-known/openid-configuration` returns the OIDC 1.0 discovery doc with `userinfo_endpoint` populated",
        "`GET /api/auth/oauth2/userinfo` returns OIDC claims (`sub`, `email`, `name`) for a bearer issued with `openid email profile` scope",
        "`GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` returns RFC 9728 §3 metadata (`resource`, `authorization_servers`, `bearer_methods_supported`)",
        "Registering an `http` loopback redirect URI with `application_type: \"native\"` returns a `client_id`",
        "The byte-identical registration body sent as `application_type: \"web\"` is refused `400 invalid_redirect_uri` — the negative control that makes -013 a statement about the native path rather than a permissive server",
        "`application_type: \"native\"` does NOT permit a routable-host `http` redirect URI — it relaxes loopback only (RFC 8252 §7)",
        "A public client (`token_endpoint_auth_method: \"none\"`) holding a genuinely valid access token is still refused `401 invalid_client` at `/api/auth/oauth2/introspect` (RFC 7662 §2.1 — refused for credentials, not token validity)",
        "`POST /api/auth/oauth2/revoke` answers `400 unsupported_token_type` for a resource-bound access token — naming a `resource` mints a self-contained signed JWT, which has no stored row to delete (RFC 7009 §2.2.1)",
        "Ending the user's session deactivates a resource-bound access token minted from it: introspection reports `active: true` before sign-out and `active: false` after (OIDC back-channel logout)",
        "The configured consent page (`consentPage: '/oauth/consent'`) renders instead of 404ing, names the client's REGISTERED redirect origin, and marks a dynamically registered client as unverified — BLOCKED ON -020 (see the ordering rule below)",
        "An anonymous `POST /api/auth/oauth2/register` is refused `401` with a `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer` challenge by default, while the byte-identical body succeeds for a signed-in user",
        "Setting `SOVRIUM_OAUTH_ANONYMOUS_CLIENT_REGISTRATION=true` re-opens anonymous registration for headless MCP deployments — the opt-in is the only difference from -020",
        "When open registration is enabled, `/api/auth/oauth2/register` is per-IP rate-limited on the same 20-per-60s sliding window as `/api/auth/sign-up/email`, returning `429` once the window closes",
        "The full PKCE-S256 `/token` round-trip (register client → authorize → exchange code) succeeds under the SQLite engine — locks the Better Auth org-plugin adapter's SQLite branch for `oauthClients` / `oauthAccessTokens` (`api/mcp/auth.ts:10,161-173` + `better-auth-routes.ts:17,436,451`)",
        "A client-resource link written with upstream's own values — the `client_id` STRING and the resource `identifier` URI — is accepted and readable by `client_id`, the lookup the plugin uses to test whether a client is already linked",
        "The join table refuses a row primary key in place of the `client_id` or the resource identifier, probed one column at a time with the other half held valid, while the same statement with both halves valid is accepted",
        "`ON DELETE CASCADE` reaches the link row through the semantic columns: deleting a client by `client_id` or a resource by `identifier` removes exactly its own links and leaves unrelated links standing",
        "`oauth_client.client_id` is unique, so a duplicate registration is refused by the database — the constraint upstream's `oauth-client-row-unique` collision handling depends on, and the prerequisite for -001's foreign key",
        "The same link contract holds on SQLite, whose mirror is a separate source file and migration — Postgres-only coverage would let a half-applied fix pass",
      ],
    },
  ],
