  "automation-runs": [
    {
      id: "US-AUTOMATIONS-OPERATIONAL-PAUSE",
      title: "Pause an automation without editing config",
      criteria: [
        "An automation that has **never run** (no `automation_definitions` row exists) can be paused; the pause is stored keyed on its config `name` and a subsequent trigger creates no run",
        "A paused **webhook** automation returns 404 to its webhook URL and creates no run; a request bearing a wrong secret also returns **404, never 401**, identically to a config-disabled automation (anti-enumeration — site 10)",
        "A paused **cron** automation creates no run across a full scheduling window; resuming it makes it run again **without a server restart** (site 4 gates at fire time; registration is deliberately not gated)",
        "A paused **record-event** automation creates no run on record insert or update, while an unpaused sibling on the same table and events runs (sites 6 and 11)",
        "A paused **form-submission** automation creates no run on form submit, while an unpaused sibling on the same form runs (site 7)",
        "A paused **auth-event** automation creates no run on sign-up, while an unpaused sibling on the same event runs (site 8)",
        "A paused **comment-event** automation creates no run when a comment is posted, while an unpaused sibling on the same table runs (site 9)",
        "A paused **manual** automation returns 404 from the manual-run endpoint and creates no run, identically to a config-disabled one (site 2)",
        "**Replaying** a historical run of a paused automation returns 404 and creates no new run, identically to a config-disabled one (site 3)",
        "A pause set before a restart is **still in force after it** — the automation creates no run on the second boot, and resuming after the restart makes it run again",
        "A **config-disabled** automation is distinct from a paused one: it reports `disabled`, resuming it does not make it run, and its pause row (if any) survives a config toggle so re-enabling in config returns it to `paused`, not `active`",
        "Pausing an automation **does not cancel a run already in progress** — an executing run completes normally, while the next trigger creates no new run",
        "Incident workflow: a webhook automation runs, is paused mid-incident, stops producing runs across webhook + record + cron paths while its sibling keeps running, survives a restart still paused, and resumes cleanly",
      ],
    },
  ],
