        "A route whose handler runs several Effect programs (`POST /api/forms/:name/submissions` runs three) still produces exactly **one** root span (empty `parentSpanId`) for one request, and every captured span shares that root's `traceId` — one request is one trace",
        "When the traces endpoint refuses the batch (a collector answering **404** on `/v1/traces`, as GlitchTip 6.2.2 does), `server.output()` carries a WARN line naming `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT` — the drop is never silent",
        "Full tracing workflow in one boot: the root `http.server` span with its attributes, a child span chaining to the root, and a log record correlated to the root's `traceId`",
        "With traces armed + full sampling, an authenticated `GET /api/tables/:tableId/records` POSTs a span batch to `/v1/traces` containing a **`db.query`** span that chains up to the root `http.server` span (of templated `route` `/api/tables/:tableId/records`) through the `tables.create-list-records-program` use-case span — itself an immediate child of the root — and carrying `operation: \"select\"` + `table` (the logical table name) attributes",
        "The same request pushes a **`db.query.duration`** histogram datapoint to `/v1/metrics` labeled `operation: \"select\"` and `table` (the logical table name), with an observation `count` ≥ 1 — the DB-query-latency instrument from the METRICS story's _Metric Set_, made testable",
        "Full DB-seam workflow in one boot: one authenticated records read yields both the `db.query` span chaining under the request root through its use-case span (with `{operation, table}` attributes) and the correlated `db.query.duration` metric datapoint (`{operation, table}` labels)",
        "With traces armed + full sampling, an authenticated `POST /api/ai/chat` POSTs a span batch to `/v1/traces` containing an **`ai.request`** child span whose `parentSpanId` equals the root `http.server` span (of templated `route` `/api/ai/chat`) and carrying `provider`, `model`, and `operation: \"chat\"` attributes",
        "The same request pushes **`ai.request.duration`** (histogram) and **`ai.request.count`** (sum) datapoints to `/v1/metrics`, each labeled `provider`, `model`, and `operation: \"chat\"`, with an observation `count` / value ≥ 1 — the AI-request instruments from the METRICS story's _Metric Set_, made testable",
        "Full AI-seam workflow in one boot: one authenticated chat turn yields both the `ai.request` child span chaining under the request root (with `{provider, model, operation}` attributes) and the correlated `ai.request.duration` + `ai.request.count` datapoints (`{provider, model, operation}` labels)",
        "With traces armed + full sampling, an authenticated `POST /api/automations/:name/trigger` (manual trigger) POSTs a span batch to `/v1/traces` containing an **`automation.run`** span that chains up to the root `http.server` span (of templated `route` `/api/automations/:name/trigger`) through the `automations.run-manual-automation` use-case span — itself an immediate child of the root — and carrying `automation` (the definition name) + `status: \"success\"` attributes",
        "The same run pushes **`automation.run.duration`** (histogram, labeled `automation`) and **`automation.run.count`** (sum, labeled `automation` + `status: \"success\"`) datapoints to `/v1/metrics`, with an observation `count` / value ≥ 1 — the automation-run instruments from the METRICS story's _Metric Set_, made testable",
