  "form-field-groups": [
    {
      id: "US-FORMS-FIELD-GROUPS",
      title: "Section Dividers in Single-Page Forms",
      criteria: [
        "`fieldGroups[]` is optional; when omitted, all fields render in source order with no section dividers",
        "When present, `fieldGroups[]` must contain at least one group; `fieldGroups[i].label` must be a non-empty string and `fieldGroups[i].fields[]` must contain at least one field name (schema-enforced)",
        "Each group accepts an optional `visibleWhen` rule. Groups without `visibleWhen` always render. Groups with `visibleWhen` render only when the rule evaluates true at render time",
        "A group's `visibleWhen.field` must be a non-empty string and `visibleWhen.operator` must be one of `eq`, `neq`, `contains`, `empty`, `notEmpty`; an unknown operator fails schema validation",
        "When a group's `visibleWhen` rule evaluates false, the group's label is hidden AND every field listed in that group's `fields[]` is hidden; hidden fields are excluded from required-field validation",
        "When `fieldGroups[]` is set, the renderer emits a section header containing each group's `label` immediately above that group's fields in `fieldGroups[]` array order. Field names listed in `fieldGroups[i].fields[]` that do NOT exist in the form's top-level `fields[]` render as no-ops (no error today; flagged for cross-validation in a Phase 2 follow-up)",
      ],
    },
  ],
  "form-fields": [
    {
      id: "US-FORMS-FIELDS",
      title: "Explicit Field List with Table-Bound and Standalone Kinds",
      criteria: [
        "A form's `fields[]` array is required, must contain at least one field, and rejects empty arrays at validation",
        "`kind: table-field` requires `column`; the column must exist on `submitTo.table` (cross-validation)",
        "`kind: table-field` is rejected when `submitTo.table` is not set on the form (validation error names both the field and the missing table)",
        "`kind: standalone` requires `name` and `inputType`; the `name` must be unique within the form's `fields[]`",
        "Across both kinds, the resolved field identifier (table-field's `column` or standalone's `name`) must be unique within the form's `fields[]`",
        "`label`, `placeholder`, `helpText` accept literal strings and Sovrium i18n keys (`$t:forms.contact.name.label`)",
        "`defaultValue` accepts a literal value matching the field's input type, or a variable expression: `$query.{name}` (URL query), `$now` (server ISO 8601 timestamp), `$user.{property}` (rejected on public forms — see access-control story)",
        "A field with `hidden: true` does not render in the UI but its `defaultValue` IS submitted with the form (typical use case: marketing attribution fields)",
        "PARTIAL — the `inputType: signature` standalone field renders a labelled `<canvas class=\"signature\">` and a base64 PNG submitted to `/api/forms/:name/submissions` is accepted and stored; the draw-and-clear capture interaction is NOT built (see the not-built note below)",
        "Type-mismatched `defaultValue` (e.g. a string default on a `number` field) fails validation with an error naming the field and its expected type",
        "A `table-field` bound to a `user`-typed column renders a picker (combobox/select with `data-field-type=\"user\"`) instead of a plain text input",
        "A `user`-typed column with `allowMultiple: true` renders a multi-select picker (emits `data-allow-multiple=\"true\"`)",
        "A required select renders an empty leading option labelled by its `placeholder`, so nothing is preselected and required blocks submission until the reader chooses",
        "A `$query` prefill or a literal `defaultValue` selects its own option, and the empty option is rendered without being selected",
        "An optional select left untouched submits empty and stores NULL rather than its first option",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "US-FORMS-INLINE-RELATIONSHIP-CREATE",
      title: "Inline Relationship Create",
      criteria: [
        "`$parent.<field>` prefill resolves the parent record's field at render time",
        "`lockPrefill: true` hides the prefilled field from the UI but submits its value",
        "`lockPrefill: false` (default) shows the field with the prefill as the initial value; user may change",
        "Multi-relationship fields prefill an array (e.g., `tags: $parent.tags`)",
        "Submit revalidates parent existence; if the parent was deleted, the request returns 422",
        "User can complete full inline-create workflow (regression)",
        "Locked `$record.id` prefill renders a hidden input with the resolved host-record id, not the literal (GAP-I2)",
        "Locked `$record.<non-id-field>` prefill resolves that column's value from the host record (GAP-I2)",
        "User can complete full `$record`-token inline-prefill workflow (regression) (GAP-I2)",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "US-FORMS-PREFILL",
      title: "Prefill Field Defaults from URL or User Context",
      criteria: [
        "`prefill` is optional; when omitted, all fields render with their schema-level defaults (or empty)",
        "A `prefill` value that is a string starting with `$` is treated as a server-resolved reference **only when it matches** the security regex documented in the Overview (`$query.<name>`, `$user.<prop>`, `$parent.<path>`, or `$record.<path>`, with a strict identifier shape after the dot). A `$`-rooted string that does NOT match a documented root (e.g. `$env.X`, `$db.users[0]`, `$query.foo-bar`, `$user.first-name`) is accepted as an opaque **literal** via the union's string fallback and rendered verbatim — never resolved against server state, never aliasing a sensitive root. The regex message is `Prefill source must be a literal value or a reference like $query.<name>, $user.<prop>, $parent.<path>, or $record.<path>`",
        "Literal string, number, or boolean values in `prefill` are accepted as fixed defaults and rendered verbatim without server-side substitution. Strings that do NOT start with `$` are always treated as literals (e.g. `priority: Medium`)",
        "`$query.<name>` references resolve from the request URL's query string at render time. When the named parameter is absent or empty, the field renders with no prefilled value (NOT the literal `$query.<name>` string)",
        "`$user.<prop>` references resolve only when the form's `access` requires authentication AND a session is present. On a form without authenticated access (or for an anonymous request to such a form), `$user.*` references resolve to empty — they do not error and do not expose unauthenticated user state. The renderer's allow-list of resolvable `<prop>` values is restricted to non-sensitive session profile fields (e.g. `id`, `email`, `name`); attempts to resolve unsupported props render empty",
        "A `$query.<name>` prefill targeting a `hidden: true` field carries the resolved value into the **submitted record** (not merely a rendered visible input): loading the form with `?ref=partnerX` and submitting stores the hidden field's column value as `partnerX`. When the param is absent the hidden field falls back to its literal `defaultValue` (or empty), and the resolved value is never exposed as an editable input",
      ],
    },
  ],
