  "form-on-success-error": [
    {
      id: "US-FORMS-ONSUCCESS-AND-ONERROR",
      title: "Post-Submit Behavior (Success Page, Redirect, Reset, Toast)",
      criteria: [
        "`onSuccess.type: successPage` replaces the rendered form with a success screen showing `title`, `message`, optional summary (when `showSummary: true`), and configured `actions[]`",
        "`onSuccess.type: redirect` navigates the submitter to `url` after `delaySeconds` (default 2); `url` may interpolate `$submission.id` and `$record.id` (submitter-provided column values via `$record.<column>` are APP-FORMS-169; `$t:` locale resolution of `url` is APP-FORMS-144)",
        "`onSuccess.type: reset` clears all fields to their `defaultValue`; with `preserveFields: [...]` the listed fields keep their submitted values for the next entry",
        "`onSuccess.type: reset` on a multi-step form returns the user to step 1 with the un-preserved fields cleared, and the server-side draft re-seeded so `preserveFields` still prefill their own later steps",
        "`onSuccess.type: toast` (the platform default) shows an in-page toast and leaves the form populated; the toast respects `variant` (`success`, `info`, `warning`, `error`)",
        "`onError.type: toast` (default) and `onError.type: message` render an error UI with the configured `message`; on validation errors the platform also surfaces inline field-level errors regardless of `onError.type`",
        "A `successPage.actions[]` entry with `action: reset` resets the form to the same state as `onSuccess.type: reset`; an entry with `action: navigate` and `url` triggers a redirect",
        "Template variable interpolation in `url`/`title`/`message` substitutes unresolved variables with empty strings (never literal `$record.id`) and logs a warning when a `$record.*` reference is used on a form whose `submitTo.table` is not set",
        "`onSuccess.redirect.url` interpolates `$record.<column>` with the **submitter-provided** value of that column on the inserted `submitTo.table` row — e.g. `url: /done?email=$record.email` resolves to `/done?email=<submitted email>`. Only columns the submitter actually supplied are interpolated (privileged / server-computed columns are never exposed); an unresolved `$record.<column>` (missing column, or a submission that wrote no bound-table row) substitutes to an empty string per APP-FORMS-068",
      ],
    },
  ],
